test-results/
# Visual baselines are generated + compared in the pinned Linux container, so
# only the committed `-linux` screenshots are authoritative. A local
# `npm run test:visual:update` on macOS/Windows writes `-darwin`/`-win32`
# baselines that must NOT be committed.
e2e/visual/__screenshots__/*-darwin.png
e2e/visual/__screenshots__/*-win32.png
scheduler.db
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# Migration backup sidecars — 0600 at-rest hardened, never committed (PR-C)
*.bak

# Secrets — never commit (the data-guard CI check enforces this too)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.p12
*.pfx
*.mobileprovision

# Project-local Cursor MCP config — never commit (#292). The managed scheduler
# key lives in the macOS Keychain, never in this file; the tracked
# `.cursor/mcp.example.json` / `.cursor/mcp.remote.example.json` carry only
# placeholders. The `mcp-config-secret-free` CI check enforces this.
.cursor/mcp.json

# machine-local continual-learning memory — never commit
agent-learnings.md
